        "description": "Edits a YAML file using path-based operations. More efficient than text-based editing\nbecause you specify YAML paths instead of large find/replace strings.\n\nSupports three operations:\n- set: Sets a value at a path (creates intermediate nodes if needed)\n- delete: Removes a value at a path (WARNING: deleting array items will shift index values)\n- insert: Inserts a value into an array at an index, shifting existing elements\n\nPath is specified as an array of strings, e.g., [\"spec\", \"containers\", \"0\", \"image\"]\n- Keys are strings: [\"metadata\", \"name\"]\n- Array indices are strings: [\"items\", \"0\"]\n- Root (entire file): empty array []\n\nFor 'set' and 'insert' operations, you must specify:\n- valueType: \"object\", \"array\", \"scalar\", or \"null\"\n- value: The raw YAML content (not required for \"null\" type)\n\nFor 'insert' operations, the path must end with an array index.\n\nExamples:\n- Set scalar: path=[\"metadata\", \"name\"], valueType=\"scalar\", value=\"my-app\"\n- Set object: path=[\"spec\"], valueType=\"object\", value=\"{replicas: 3}\"\n- Set array: path=[\"items\"], valueType=\"array\", value=\"[a, b, c]\"\n- Set null: path=[\"metadata\", \"annotations\"], valueType=\"null\"\n- Insert at index 0: path=[\"items\", \"0\"], valueType=\"scalar\", value=\"new-first\"\n- Insert in middle: path=[\"steps\", \"2\"], valueType=\"object\", value=\"{name: new-step}\"\n\nThis tool supports multiple edits (one per operation entry in the operations list). It is recommended to\nALWAYS perform multiple edits in one tool call instead of calling one edit at a time, as this is slow\nand extremely wasteful on tokens passing context back and forth"
